  <section>
    <h2>1. Information collected</h2>
    <p>We do not ask you to submit personal information. There are no accounts, contact forms, comment fields, bookings or payments on this site, and we do not maintain a visitor database. Some data is nevertheless processed automatically when a page loads:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (property G-HXM22WWPKP) loads on every page, including legal pages, and may use cookies to process page views, browser/device information and usage events.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> delivers the site and processes connection and security data. Depending on hosting settings, a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon may record visits, page views, URL paths, referrers and performance dimensions.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Maps</strong> is embedded as a frame in the map section. Google may receive your IP address, browser/device information and map interactions, and may set its own cookies.</li>
      <li><strong>Weather data</strong> is fetched by the server from Open-Meteo for fixed approximate lake-area coordinates. Your device location is not sent to that service by this guide.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No precise device location is collected and no location permission is requested. The dated Google Maps rating shown in the guide is a manually checked third-party snapshot, not information collected from you.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. How information is used</h2>
    <p>Analytics and hosting data serve only to understand aggregate traffic and keep the site available. We do not sell personal data, do not use it for advertising, profiling or newsletters, and do not make automated decisions about visitors. Each third-party provider processes data under its own policy, not under an agreement with a park operator.</p>
    <p>The weather panel, route suggestions and planning notes are informational. They are not observations at the entrance, safety clearances or operating notices.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics is enabled by default and this guide provides no consent banner or on-page switch. Cloudflare and the embedded Google Maps frame may set their own cookies as described above. See <a href="/cookie-settings">Cookie settings</a> for the categories and the browser-level controls available to you.</p>
    <p>The registered service worker only removes this guide's legacy caches. It does not intercept requests, store personal data or provide an offline forecast.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Data security and retention</h2>
    <p>Pages are served over HTTPS. No method of transmission or storage can be guaranteed completely secure, so we cannot promise absolute security.</p>
    <p>This guide stores no visitor database and defines no retention period of its own. Retention of analytics, hosting and map data follows the policies of Google, Cloudflare and the other providers named here. The guide itself does not offer a data export or deletion request channel because it holds no visitor records.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Third parties, children and changes</h2>
    <p>External links — the municipal council, provincial tourism pages, railway and transport bodies, and the Google Maps place link — lead to services with their own data practices. Relevant provider information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy</a>, <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/high-level-metrics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare metrics</a>, <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open-Meteo terms</a>.</p>
    <p>This guide is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect their data. We may revise this page when the site's services change; the date at the top shows the latest revision. For the guide's factual verification date, see the <a href="/#sources">Sources section</a>.</p>
  </section>
